COMMERCIAL LICENSE AGREEMENT

This Commercial License governs the use of BrewGraph software by parties who
do not wish to comply with the obligations of the GNU General Public License
v3.0 — primarily the requirement to publish your full source code.

WHO NEEDS THIS LICENSE?

You must obtain a Commercial License if you:

  • Distribute BrewGraph (or a derivative work) in a product or service
    WITHOUT releasing your full source code under GPL v3

  • Are a company, business entity, or organization distributing BrewGraph
    in any quantity

  • Embed BrewGraph into a SaaS product or commercial hosted service

  • Sell products containing BrewGraph on any marketplace (AliExpress,
    Amazon, eBay, Tindie, etc.)

WHAT THE COMMERCIAL LICENSE GRANTS

Upon execution of a written agreement with the Licensor, the Licensee receives:

  ✓ The right to incorporate BrewGraph into proprietary, closed-source
    products without triggering GPL v3 source disclosure obligations

  ✓ The right to distribute such products commercially without quantity limits

  ✓ The right to modify BrewGraph without publishing those modifications

  ✓ The right to operate BrewGraph as part of a hosted SaaS service

  ✓ A royalty-free license for the agreed scope and term as defined in the
    signed agreement

REQUIREMENTS UNDER COMMERCIAL LICENSE

The Licensee must:

  1. Retain all "Copyright (c) Magnus Persson" notices in source code and
     documentation

  2. Display a copyright notice in any "About", "System Info", or equivalent
     screen in the product UI:
         "Portions copyright (c) Magnus Persson — https://github.com/mp-se/brewgraph"

  3. Not sublicense, resell, or transfer the Commercial License rights
     to any third party without prior written consent from the Licensor

  4. Not misrepresent the origin of the software or remove attribution

